    description: "compact's default output seeds connectivity selection by (-confidence, symbol_id) (compact.py near line 1407), so any change to an entry kind's confidence reorders the seeds and changes which nodes make the cut. PR 4 (WI-fupap) raised main to 0.95 in Go, Java, Rust, C, C#, Kotlin and Scala, and the 100-node compact output then differed on 9 of 12 repositories, by 7 to 38 nodes. On alertmanager, 22 of 100 nodes differ.\n\nUnchanged repositories: lazygit, mini-redis, ripgrep, sqlalchemy.\n\nQuestion: should compact seed in the same total entry order the entry-point list uses (kind rank, then the existing tie keys), so that a confidence recalibration cannot reshuffle compact on its own? Confidence is a probability that a symbol IS an entry; it is not a rank of how central it is.\n\nRepro: `hypergumbo compact --input <map>` on alertmanager in both arms. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr4/fupap/out/*.compact.ids and RESULTS.md."  # 3086
    fields: {}  # 3086
